    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0229" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg113"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/803.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The advance loan has been agreed to upon the following among other conditions:
                    that the banks have option to provide further advances for monthly requirements
                    of the Chinese Government, which shall assure to the groups option of
                    undertaking reorganization loan.</p>
                <p>In note of March 9, Yuan agreed to these conditions, but on the 14th Tong signed
                    a loan with a Belgian-Russian group for £1,000,000 at 97 and 5 per cent
                    interest, with Kalgan Railway revenues as security and option on £10,000,000
                    loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
